  "explanation": {
    "short": "Four more vowel shapes you will see everywhere: ือ (a throaty \"uh\"), ัว (like \"oo-a\"), เ◌ีย (like \"ee-a\") and อ on its own (like \"aw\" in \"saw\").",
    "more": "The shapes wrap around the consonant: in ชื่อ and ดื่ม the vowel sign ื sits above and the tone mark goes above it, so it can look crowded. In ซื้อ the mark ้ sits on a low-class ซ and so gives a high tone. The letter อ is two things: a silent consonant that holds a vowel (อา, อ่าน) and, after another consonant, the vowel \"aw\" (ขอ, รอ). Same letter, but you can tell which by where it stands."
  },
